0..77 Comment "/// This source states that each nesting of one path chain has one composite."
78..81 Comment "///"
82..138 Comment "/// The unbiased composite does not select a bracketing."
139..203 Comment "/// A proof therefore uses `Path.here` instead of an associator."
204..207 Comment "///"
208..282 Comment "/// Evaluation and the kernel move each transport through the chain paths."
283..331 Comment "/// They reach the left-nested `Path.step` fold."
